/-
Fmt/M2Theirs.lean: the public data of the programs' own files of the second toy, and the two
descriptions under which their proof files are read. "Theirs": the programs' own files of the second
toy.

Test data, with tests that compare the parameter bytes with the bytes that this library spells from
the public file and the protocol's sizes (the record `Par` of Fmt/M2Types.lean).

Sources. This file was generated by a program from files in the archive
toy-files-made-by-the-cuts-tools.tgz (sha256
f97d6774317660e9033841ab36ce4e63e376ebeb25542cf6f1f92e8f61644aa1), which the programs (the C++
implementation that comes with this Lean code) made for the second toy (a chain of three links;
Fmt/M2Dec.lean says what it is). The data are made-up toy data: no model and no weights. Taken from
the archive (the archive is not in this repository): honest-and-altered/links/links.parameters,
.configuration, .digests.tsv; honest-and-altered/links/tiny-links.parameters, .configuration,
.digests.tsv; honest-and-altered/links/tiny-with-a-repeat/tiny-links.digests.tsv. The set with a
repeated position has the parameter bytes and the public file of the tiny parameters, byte for byte
(checked by the generating program). The generating program stops unless every file that the
archive's own list of checksums (SUMS) names, the lists among them, has the sha256 given there. The
file imports no Mathlib.





1. What the file contains.
   `full`, `tiny`: the parameter bytes at full parameters and at tiny parameters.
   `pubFull`, `pubTiny`: the one public file of each.
   `specFull`, `specTiny`: the two descriptions (a description is what a verifier knows before it
     sees a file: label, parameter bytes, statement, rounds): `specOf` (Fmt/M2Plan.lean) at the
     sizes `toyPar`, `tinyPar` (Fmt/M2Types.lean), the digest of the public file, and the parameter
     items `itemsOf` (Fmt/M2Items.lean). Proof files are read at these terms.
   `printedFull`, `printedTiny`, `printedRepeat`: five values that the programs print for each of
     the three sets of files, in base 16: the digest of the public file, the digest of the
     parameters, the chain's random bytes, the run value, the first chain value.

2. What is checked when the file compiles (#guard). The lengths of the four byte strings. The
   parameter bytes that Lean spells from the sizes and the public file are the programs' bytes, byte
   for byte, at both sizes. Both descriptions are admissible (`Spec.ok`) and have 76 and 58 rounds.
   The programs' bytes can be read (Fmt/ParamsRead.lean), and the digest of the public file and the
   items found in them are this library's. The two digests equal the printed ones. (The random
   bytes, the run value and the first chain value are compared with what the reader computes from
   the proof files in Fmt/M2EngineLF.lean, M2EngineLT.lean, M2EngineLR.lean.)

3. Theorems. None in this file. `Spec.ok` at these two descriptions is also a theorem
   (Fmt/M2SpecKnown.lean), and the sizes and the description can be read back from the bytes that
   Lean spells (Fmt/M2ParOf.lean, Fmt/M2SpecBack.lean).

4. What is not claimed.
   No theorem. The tests (#guard) are evaluations that Lean makes when the file compiles. They speak
   of these bytes and of nothing else. In particular, that Lean's bytes are the programs' bytes is a
   test on these files, not a theorem.
   Nothing is said here about any proof file.

Terms: lean/GLOSSARY.md.
-/
import Fmt.M2Items
import Fmt.ParamsRead

namespace Fmt
namespace M2
namespace Theirs

/-- the parameter bytes of the programs' run at full size, as they came -/
def full : ByteArray := cat [
  unhex "",
  unhex "",
  unhex "",
  unhex "",
  unhex ""]
/-- the parameter bytes of their tiny run -/
def tiny : ByteArray := cat [
  unhex "",
  unhex "",
  unhex "",
  unhex ""]
/-- the one public file of each -/
def pubFull : ByteArray := unhex ""
def pubTiny : ByteArray := unhex ""

/-- The two descriptions. -/
def specFull : Spec := specOf toyPar (configDigest [pubFull]) (itemsOf toyPar)
def specTiny : Spec := specOf tinyPar (configDigest [pubTiny]) (itemsOf tinyPar)

/-- what they print for a run: the configuration's digest, the parameters' digest, the chain's
random bytes, the run's value, the chain's first value -/
def printedFull : String × String × String × String × String :=
  ("243697d0866750794a648ce915dd7da1c94408b77a9eadacce5e2a2cd872757a",
    "9b25d5f4e5adf08c456bf0cbd7ba184a7ce04c5b54e8ddb311a9c8fdbb365aab",
    "fbe06ca1818d76a63a8190febcbbc326c74f2e37c72831cc35a7f08d16ce47f1",
    "bdea474c5ca6f1aa72d8c58d11344190eb699d953eee6839d0b520943a9199fd",
    "65b38fcabc733d5a000aecd98f96edf3578c4bd932164eee0cc4ac86c852e2d3")
def printedTiny : String × String × String × String × String :=
  ("27d791a36fff70de9c37b638550e3a2daf85a40aeb723fd8362bb18d60704126",
    "59922437150dbd2232f5986d9c1b939e1639a1e7b145989202984f34a08c1161",
    "b4903a441c997b1811b4a5b3ce1d4886e9ec3cb52245271153a673a7351682a7",
    "2f20ebc3f2572053560824fe456c0a19a30f389ac5a682c96938cf8917760c05",
    "d904e818cc09c1b2f30e2efb196f9a552b4dba274ac4c32ce097e4b65fcd3821")
def printedRepeat : String × String × String × String × String :=
  ("27d791a36fff70de9c37b638550e3a2daf85a40aeb723fd8362bb18d60704126",
    "59922437150dbd2232f5986d9c1b939e1639a1e7b145989202984f34a08c1161",
    "938e259a1e307c5a896f3b4b4a05bf6ec9c90e2a3fc95d3bc0f1528fff04be70",
    "452cb612ca3409d66c6d8dcebebcfc88981bbc64be805782c9251633868f25a3",
    "e1a3f16236fc03a4af52d543ae5b32ff66db37ba1c012bdc7301d1ca865616cc")

end Theirs

#guard Theirs.full.size = 8744 && Theirs.tiny.size = 6878 && Theirs.pubFull.size = 186 && Theirs.pubTiny.size = 237
-- their bytes, spelled by this library
#guard Theirs.specFull.params = Theirs.full && Theirs.specTiny.params = Theirs.tiny
#guard Theirs.specFull.ok && Theirs.specTiny.ok && Theirs.specFull.rounds.length = 76 && Theirs.specTiny.rounds.length = 58
-- their bytes are read; configuration and items are this library's
#guard ((paramsRead Theirs.full).map fun p => (decide (p.cfg = configDigest [Theirs.pubFull]), decide (p.others = itemsOf toyPar))) = some (true, true)
#guard ((paramsRead Theirs.tiny).map fun p => (decide (p.cfg = configDigest [Theirs.pubTiny]), decide (p.others = itemsOf tinyPar))) = some (true, true)
-- the two digests as they print them
#guard (hex (configDigest [Theirs.pubFull]), hex (paramsDigest Theirs.full)) = (Theirs.printedFull.1, Theirs.printedFull.2.1)
#guard (hex (configDigest [Theirs.pubTiny]), hex (paramsDigest Theirs.tiny)) = (Theirs.printedTiny.1, Theirs.printedTiny.2.1) && (Theirs.printedRepeat.1, Theirs.printedRepeat.2.1) = (Theirs.printedTiny.1, Theirs.printedTiny.2.1)

end M2
end Fmt
